From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] shell: focus the compositor when an Activity view is shown

The shell switches its GTK4 stack to the "activity" page without ever giving
the Casilda compositor widget GTK keyboard focus. Nothing else on that page
can hold focus - the embedded Activity is a separate Wayland client, opaque
to this process's focus chain - so the focused widget stays wherever Home or
Journal left it. Grab focus on the compositor at both switch points.

---
 src/jarabe/model/shell.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/src/jarabe/model/shell.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/model/shell.py
@@ -509,6 +509,7 @@ class ShellModel(Gtk.Application):
                 self.stack.set_visible_child_name("journal")
             else:
                 self.stack.set_visible_child_name("activity")
+                self.compositor.grab_focus()
         else:
             self.stack.set_visible_child_name("home")

@@ -518,6 +519,7 @@ class ShellModel(Gtk.Application):
                 self.stack.set_visible_child_name("journal")
             else:
                 self.stack.set_visible_child_name("activity")
+                self.compositor.grab_focus()

     def _get_activities_with_window(self):
         ret = []
